{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head fd8a12efd7f5e4aba1c20b758896f97e4cc7a90f after seeing request d8b2b7a6f6415352b4cce46c676b0f4f45e89d13, which rests on this head's internal/app artifact and proposes a later production staleness-boundary change; it does not contradict this test-only patch. Architecture: only test infrastructure changes. internal/testgit remains the shared hermetic Git seam and the four heavy packages gain top-level scheduling annotations; no production layer, API, storage, or transport contract changes. Security: GIT_TEMPLATE_DIR is installed only by TestMain in test processes; core.fsync=none and gc.auto=0 therefore affect throwaway repositories, while application durability assertions still exercise os.File.Sync. The production ambient-template exposure recorded separately is unchanged. Tests that mutate environment, capture process-wide output, measure time or allocations, or replace package hooks remain serial; my race run across internal/kernel, internal/app, internal/service, and cmd/gs passed. Simplification: the single template configuration avoids scattered per-command overrides, and top-level t.Parallel uses Go's existing serial/parallel barrier rather than a custom scheduler. I found no unnecessary production seam or weaker smaller change. Independent race timings were kernel 85.164s, app 70.613s, service 24.099s, and cmd/gs 246.986s.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:25846bf6b9c44bf3ec6c04b3762d78447a042aaa","head":"fd8a12efd7f5e4aba1c20b758896f97e4cc7a90f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d8b2b7a6f6415352b4cce46c676b0f4f45e89d13\",\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7f3132008439e9650eefc35851c794ffc87028d1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4853315d16f0ca905be5a4680f1902a5c925f937","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}